y and doesn't connect to its servers. The optional overlay is a separate window that only shows public information or what can be worked out from what has been played, never hidden information."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What data does it send?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Your games, screenshots and statistics stay in a folder on your PC. The program only downloads the updated meta deck lists, one per format (every 3 days), looks up card names on Scryfall (also with Magic Online ids) when it needs them, and asks GitHub once a day whether there's a new version. You can turn all three off in Settings. It sends data out only when you ask for something. The AI analysis sends that game's data (result, deck, hands, cards seen and timeline), never your name or the opponent's. A bug report sends what you write, your email if you add one, the ManaLab version, your system and language, whether you use Arena or Magic Online, an anonymous ID of your PC and, if you tick it, the last lines of registro.log with your user name and codes removed. It sends no games or decks."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Windows says «Windows protected your PC». Is it safe?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "That warning appears for programs without a paid code-signing certificate, which is common for small free tools. Click «More info» and then «Run anyway». It only shows on the first download: new versions install with «Update now» from inside the app, with no warning. To avoid it the first time too, before unzipping right-click the ZIP › Properties › tick «Unblock» › OK. Every version is checked on VirusTotal before it's published."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does it work on Mac or Linux?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "For now it's for Windows 10 and 11. There is no native Linux version, and it has not been tested with Wine or Proton, so we can't promise it will work."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is it free?", "accepted