<body>
{{> cabecera_en 1=e}}
<main id="inicio">
<section class="portada">
<div class="envoltura">
<div>
<div class="eti">Free Magic Online (MTGO) tracker</div>
<h1>Your Magic Online games, <em>saved on their own.</em></h1>
<p class="sub">ManaLab reads Magic Online&#x27;s log while you play and keeps your opening hands, mulligans, play or draw, the opponent&#x27;s deck and your sideboard changes. Then it shows where you win and lose.</p>
<div class="nota-desc"><span>The app is free. Only the AI analysis is paid</span><span>Your data stays on your PC unless you ask for AI</span><span>Nothing to set up</span></div>
<div class="desc-bloque" id="descargar">
<p style="margin-top:14px"><a class="boton prim" href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases/download/v2.3.0/ManaLab-2.3.0-portable.zip" download data-descarga data-goatcounter-click="descarga" data-goatcounter-title="descarga-mtgo-en" id="enlace-descarga" rel="noopener"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 4v11m0 0-4.5-4.5M12 15l4.5-4.5M5 20h14"></path></svg><span>Download free</span></a></p>
<p class="nota-descarga">Version <span data-version>2.3.0</span> · ZIP · <a href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases" rel="noopener">other versions</a></p>
<template id="bloque-movil"><div class="movil-caja">
<h4 class="movil-tit">ManaLab runs on your computer</h4>
<p class="movil-txt">Send yourself the link and download it there.</p>
<p><button class="boton prim" data-compartir data-copiado="Link copied" data-titulo="compartir-movil-en" data-url="https://manalab.es/magic-online/" type="button"><span>Send me the link</span></button></p>
<p class="movil-zip"><a href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases/download/v2.3.0/ManaLab-2.3.0-portable.zip" download data-descarga data-titulo="descarga-movil-en" rel="noopener">Download the ZIP anyway</a></p>
<p aria-live="polite" class="movil-estado" role="status"></p>
</div></template>
<p class="nota-smartscreen">Requirements: Windows 10 or 11. Unzip the file and open ManaLab.exe. Nothing to install.</p>
<p class="nota-smartscreen" data-solo-pc>Before unzipping, right-click the ZIP › Properties › tick <b>Unblock</b> › OK. If a warning still appears, click <b>More info › Run anyway</b>.</p>
<p class="nota-smartscreen"><a href="/safety/">Is it safe? Check it yourself →</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="hero-medio">
<div class="ventana"><picture><source srcset="../img/en_mtgo_panel.webp" type="image/webp"><img alt="ManaLab Dashboard with Arena listening and Magic Online in a game, reading mtgo.log, and the latest matches with an MTGO tag, shown with sample data" class="cap" height="860" src="../img/en_mtgo_panel.jpg" width="1366"/></picture></div>
<p class="pie-captura" style="margin:0">Screenshot with sample data.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="guarda">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">What it saves</div>
<h2>Every Magic Online game, with what explains it</h2>
<p>Nothing to write down: it all comes from the log while you play.</p>
</div>
<div class="funciones cinco">
<div class="funcion"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 6h16M4 12h10M4 18h7"></path></svg>
<h3>Opening hands</h3>
<p>The hand you were dealt and the one you kept, in every game.</p></div>
<div class="funcion"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 4v16M4 12h16"></path></svg>
<h3>Mulligans</h3>
<p>How many you took in each game.</p></div>
<div class="funcion"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 7h13l-3-3M20 17H7l3 3"></path></svg>
<h3>Play or draw</h3>
<p>Who went first in each game, so your statistics can split by play and draw.</p></div>
<div class="funcion"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 8v4l2.5 2.5M12 4a8 8 0 1 0 0 16 8 8 0 0 0 0-16z"></path></svg>
<h3>Opponent's deck</h3>
<p>It compares the opponent's cards with the most played decks of the game's format and names the closest one. If nothing clearly matches, it is named by its colors.</p></div>
<div class="funcion"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"></path></svg>
<h3>Replay</h3>
<p>Every game step by step, with the real cards. Phases and tapped cards are deduced and marked ≈.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="banquillo">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="novedades uno">
<div class="novedad">
<div class="ventana"><picture><source srcset="../img/en_mtgo_banquillo.webp" type="image/webp"><img alt="ManaLab sideboard notice for Magic Online between games: «Did you change your sideboard?» with the buttons «Use this change», «No changes» and «Edit», shown with sample data" height="440" loading="lazy" src="../img/en_mtgo_banquillo.jpg" width="1000"/></picture></div>
<div class="cuerpo"><div class="eti">Sideboard</div>
<h2 style="font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,36px);line-height:1.12;margin:12px 0 12px">Confirm your sideboard in one click</h2>
<p>Magic Online doesn&#x27;t send your sideboarded list in time, so between games a small notice asks «Did you change your sideboard?» with three buttons: «Use this change» repeats what you did last time, «No changes» keeps your list as it is and «Edit» opens the editor.</p>
<p>Until you confirm, the overlay shows «Unconfirmed list» and the chances of drawing each card are approximate (marked ≈).</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="lee">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">What it reads</div>
<h2>It only reads files on your PC</h2>
</div>
<div class="mtgo-caja sola">
<p>These are the files ManaLab reads. It doesn't change them:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>mtgo.log</code>: the log Magic Online writes while you play. There is nothing to turn on.</li>
<li><code>Match_GameLog_*.dat</code>: the log of each game.</li>
<li><code>mtgo_game_history</code>: Magic Online's own match history.</li>
<li><code>grouping *.xml</code>: the deck files.</li>
</ul>
<p>It doesn't modify Magic Online, doesn't read its memory and doesn't connect to its servers. <a href="/safety/#lee">What it reads and how to check it →</a></p>
<p>Screenshots of your opening hand, mulligans and result are on by default and stay on your PC. You can turn them off in Settings, with a separate switch for Magic Online. If you played with ManaLab closed, you can import an <code>mtgo.log</code> file.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="tener-en-cuenta">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">Keep in mind</div>
<h2>What to keep in mind</h2>
</div>
<div class="mtgo-caja sola">
<ul>
<li><b>Your deck takes its Magic Online name</b> when the list matches exactly; otherwise it is named by its colors.</li>
<li><b>Phases and tapped cards are deduced.</b> Magic Online doesn't send them, so ManaLab works them out from the log. In the replay they are marked ≈ because they may not be exact.</li>
<li><b>The overlay can show less information</b> when the log has no table state.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="preguntas">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec"><div class="eti">FAQ</div><h2>Before you start</h2></div>
<div class="preguntas">
<details><summary>Does it work with Magic Online?</summary>
<p>Yes, from 2.3. ManaLab saves your Magic Online (MTGO) games: hands, mulligans, play or draw, the opponent&#x27;s deck, statistics, replay and overlay. There is nothing to set up: it starts by itself when you open Magic Online, and you can import an mtgo.log file. Magic Online doesn&#x27;t send turn phases or tapped cards, so ManaLab works them out from the log, and in the replay anything worked out is marked ≈ because it may not be exact. Magic Online doesn&#x27;t give your sideboarded list in time either: ManaLab asks you to confirm your changes between games with one click, and until you do the overlay shows the list as unconfirmed. The overlay can show less information when the log has no table state. Your deck takes the name you saved it with in Magic Online when the list matches exactly; otherwise it is named by its colors.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does it touch the game or give me an advantage in a match?</summary>
<p>No. It only reads the files Magic Online writes on your PC (mtgo.log, Match_GameLog_*.dat, mtgo_game_history and the grouping *.xml deck files), without modifying them. It doesn&#x27;t modify Magic Online, doesn&#x27;t read its memory and doesn&#x27;t connect to its servers. The optional overlay is a separate window that only shows public information or what can be worked out from what has been played, never hidden information.</p><p>More details: <a href="/safety/#lee">Is ManaLab safe?</a></p></details>
<details><summary>What data does it send?</summary>
<p>Your games, screenshots and statistics stay in a folder on your PC. The program only downloads the updated meta deck lists, one per format (every 3 days), looks up card names on Scryfall (also with Magic Online ids) when it needs them, and asks GitHub once a day whether there&#x27;s a new version. You can turn all three off in Settings. It sends data out only when you ask for something. The AI analysis sends that game&#x27;s data (result, deck, hands, cards seen and timeline), never your name or the opponent&#x27;s. A bug report sends what you write, your email if you add one, the ManaLab version, your system and language, whether you use Arena or Magic Online, an anonymous ID of your PC and, if you tick it, the last lines of registro.log with your user name and codes removed. It sends no games or decks.</p><p>More details: <a href="/safety/">Is ManaLab safe?</a></p></details>
<details><summary>Windows says «Windows protected your PC». Is it safe?</summary>
<p>That warning appears for programs without a paid code-signing certificate, which is common for small free tools. Click «More info» and then «Run anyway». It only shows on the first download: new versions install with «Update now» from inside the app, with no warning. To avoid it the first time too, before unzipping right-click the ZIP › Properties › tick «Unblock» › OK. Every version is checked on VirusTotal before it&#x27;s published.</p><p>More details: <a href="/safety/">Is ManaLab safe?</a></p></details>
<details><summary>Does it work on Mac or Linux?</summary>
<p>For now it&#x27;s for Windows 10 and 11. There is no native Linux version, and it has not been tested with Wine or Proton, so we can&#x27;t promise it will work.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is it free?</summary>
<p>The program is free and needs no account. The only paid part is the AI loss analysis: 5 € per month, which pays for the AI service it uses. Every other feature is free.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I get the AI analysis?</summary>
<p>Subscribe on Ko-fi (5 € per month). After paying you receive a subscription code by email. Paste it in Settings › Team and AI and the analysis appears in each lost game&#x27;s Analysis tab. Want to try it first? Ask for a free trial by <a href="mailto:manalab.app@gmail.com">email</a>.</p></details>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="apoyo">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="apoyo uno">
<div>
<div class="eti">Free to download</div>
<h2>The app is free. Only the AI analysis is paid</h2>
<p>The AI analysis of your lost games costs 5 € a month and pays for the AI service it uses. Everything else, including everything on this page, is free.</p>
<p>Want to try it first? Ask for a free trial by <a href="mailto:manalab.app@gmail.com">email</a>.</p>
<div class="acciones" style="margin-top:18px"><a class="boton prim" href="#descargar"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 4v11m0 0-4.5-4.5M12 15l4.5-4.5M5 20h14"></path></svg><span>Download free</span></a><a class="enlace-sec" href="/#ia">About the AI analysis</a></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</main>
{{> pie_en 2=b}}

<script defer="" src="/descarga.js"></script>
<script data-goatcounter="https://manalab.goatcounter.com/count" async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script></body>
</html>
